  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/shutterstock_240500314.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Over the last few weeks, cryptocurrency markets have fallen in value as most of these assets reached all-time price highs three months ago. Despite the price drops, 2021 has still been an explosive year for crypto gains and fiat-pegged stablecoins have grown massively as well. 53 days ago, the entire capitalization of fiat stablecoins crossed the $100 billion mark, and the stablecoin market valuation continues to grow, swelling 13% since the end of May.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Stablecoin Market Valuation Grows by 13% in 30 Days, Tether Issuance Slows
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Stablecoins have made their mark in the crypto economy over the last five years as these fiat-pegged tokens have grown immensely during that time period. While digital currency markets have dipped in value, the use of stablecoins has remained frothy and today the market capitalization of all the stablecoins in existence is $113 billion.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Of course, tether (USDT) is the largest stablecoin in terms of market valuation and the amount of transactions the stablecoin network processes daily. At the time of writing, the market capitalization of tether (USDT) is $62 billion and USDT’s overall valuation is 4.94% of the entire market valuation of all the crypto coins in existence.
  </p><figure id="attachment_475028" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-475028" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/foot55-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/foot55-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/foot55-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/foot55.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-475028 size-full" title="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/foot55.jpg" alt="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" width="1280" height="720" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-475028" class="wp-caption-text">Top ten stablecoins by market valuation on Friday, July 16, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Coingecko statistics show tether commands $43.5 billion in global swaps on Friday, but messari.io data shows “real volume” is around $12.51 billion. Either way you look at it, tether has more volume than BTC and ETH markets combined.
  </p><figure id="attachment_475026" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-475026" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btceth-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btceth-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btceth-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btceth.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-475026 size-full" title="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/btceth.jpg" alt="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" width="1280" height="720" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-475026" class="wp-caption-text">Tether captures more than 62% of today’s BTC trades and 51.4% of ETH trades on Friday. BUSD commands 4.5% of today’s BTC trades and 7.9% of ETH swaps on Friday as well.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Moreover, most of the BTC and ETH trades are swapped for tether (USDT) as BTC statistics show USDT captures 62.48% of today’s share of trades. The stablecoin BUSD, issued by Binance, captures 4.61% of bitcoin (BTC) swaps and is just under the U.S. dollar as BTC’s third-largest trading pair, according to cryptocompare.com data.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Tether was growing exponentially from July 2020 up until June 2021, when issuing tethers started to slow down at $61.7 billion. At the start of June, usd coin (USDC) went from $22 billion to mid-July’s $26.5 billion market capitalization.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    6 Stablecoins Saw Double and Triple-Digit Growth Last Month
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    At the start of June, the Binance stablecoin BUSD’s valuation went from $8.72 billion to $11.25 billion. In fact, most of the last 30 days of stablecoin growth can be attributed to non-tether stablecoins like USDC, BUSD, DAI, PAX, TUSD, HUSD, GUSD, and LUSD.
  </p><figure id="attachment_475029" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-475029" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/stablesss-300x123.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/stablesss-768x315.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/stablesss-1024x420.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/stablesss.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-475029 size-full" title="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/stablesss.jpg" alt="Stablecoins Swelled by $13B In 30 Days, Capture 67% of Today's Crypto Trade Volume" width="1280" height="525" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-475029" class="wp-caption-text">Stablecoin market valuation on Friday, July 16, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Out of all the well known fiat-pegged tokens, GUSD saw the largest 30-day growth, gaining 56.7%, and the synthetix.io stablecoin SUSD has seen 37.7% growth during the last month.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    BUSD grew by double digits adding 18.9% in 30 days and usd coin (USDC) rose 10.7% in that time span. Three relatively unknown stablecoins saw very large supply increases. The stablecoin defi dollar (DUSD) increased by 257.5% last month, and it was followed by empty set dollar (ESD) which jumped 129%, and frax (FRAX) which increased by over 98%.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Statistics from Coingecko show that combined, the dozens of stablecoins in existence today command $49.5 billion out of Friday’s $82.9 billion in crypto trades worldwide.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about the growth of stablecoins over the last 30 days? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
